HP's System Updates app.

com.palm.app.updates 1.1.0 as it is on the reference TouchPad (webOS CE 3.1.0), copied from
/usr/palm/applications on 2026-11-07. Copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard; never released
under an open licence; distributed by Lunacy as abandonware, like Mojo and the Prelude fonts.
codepoet asked for it, 2026-11-07, with GitHub's releases as the source of updates.

It talks to Lunacy's update service (palm://com.palm.update, AndroidLuna's UpdateService.kt),
which checks webOSArchive/Lunacy's releases on GitHub: "Your device is up to date.", or
"Lunacy 0.9.4 is now available. It's about 85MB." with Learn More, which opens the release
page in Android's browser. Lunacy never downloads or installs itself.

Lunacy's changes, marked [Lunacy] in the source:

- app/UpdateStatus.js: for a Lunacy release, the note under the version says Learn More
  opens its release page, in place of Palm's notes about downloading over the next few days.
- app/UpdateProgress.js: for a Lunacy release the button says Learn More, not Download Now,
  since it opens the release page (codepoet).
- app/UpdatesApp.js: the button and pill are no wider than a phone's card, less the
  column's margins.
- app/UpdateWebView.js: the release notes are the GitHub release's own (as plain text), not
  pages on help.palm.com, which is gone.
